-- title:
--   SL₂(K) is generated by torus, shears and Weyl element
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and consider the special linear group $\mathrm{SL}(2,K)$ of $2\times 2$ matrices of determinant $1$ over $K$. Three subsets of $\mathrm{SL}(2,K)$ are formed, described through the underlying matrix of an element: first, the set of those $g$ whose matrix equals $!![a,0;0,a^{-1}]$ for some $a\in K$ (the determinant condition forces $a\neq 0$, so this is the diagonal torus $\operatorname{diag}(a,a^{-1})$); second, the set of those $g$ whose matrix equals $!![1,z;0,1]$ for some $z\in K$, the upper unipotent shears; third, the singleton consisting of the element whose matrix is $!![0,1;-1,0]$, the Weyl element. The assertion is that the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}(2,K)$ generated by the union of these three sets is the whole group, i.e. `Subgroup.closure` of that union equals $\top$. No hypothesis on $K$ beyond being a field is imposed; in particular the field may be finite or of characteristic $2$, where the Weyl element coincides with its negative.
--
--   This is the subgroup-generation form of the Bruhat decomposition for $\mathrm{SL}_2$ over a field: every element lies in the big cell $N T w N$ or in the Borel $N T$. It is used in the treatment of automorphic forms, where a property of a function on $\mathrm{SL}(2,K)$-translates need only be verified on these three families of elements, as in the two non-existence statements about smooth cusp realizations that cite it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Matrix_SpecialLinearGroup_closure_diagonal_unipotent_weyl_eq_top.lean

import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup
import Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Subgroup.Lattice

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open scoped MatrixGroups

theorem Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.closure_diagonal_unipotent_weyl_eq_top
    {K : Type*} [Field K] :
    Subgroup.closure
      ({g : SL(2, K) | ∃ a : K, (g : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) K) = !![a, 0; 0, a⁻¹]} ∪
        {g : SL(2, K) | ∃ z : K, (g : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) K) = !![1, z; 0, 1]} ∪
        {g : SL(2, K) | (g : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) K) = !![0, 1; -1, 0]}) = ⊤ := by sorry
